  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nSurface high pressure will move east tonight ahead of a weak mid \nlevel s/w. This s/w will be undercutting a l/w ridge, which will\nhamper any deeper development of s/w and associated vorticity. Light\nand scattered rainfall with this system will end early Monday morning\nas the mean s/w axis exits to the easts during this time. The l/w\nridge builds back in Mon night and early Tues, then gets shunted ewd\nduring the day. This will allow swly flow over the Ohio Valley to\ntake hold ahead of a potent l/w trough. \n\nThis l/w trough and/or cutoff low is all over the map for Tues night\nonward, leading to very low confidence in forecast going forward. \nEven though confidence is low on mass fields, they all support rain\non Wed with deep sw flow being wrung out over the region. A continued\nchance of rain through the end of the week is also prudent given the\ndivergence of upper level mass fields. While some chance of rain is \nexpected through the period, it won't be any washout or extended \nrainfall event after the more widespread rain expected Wednesday.",
